   "meaning_mnemonic": "When a vocab is a single kanji all alone, it usually has the same meaning as its kanji parent. That goes for this vocab word as well. <kanji>Person</kanji> is <vocabulary>person</vocabulary>.",
   "reading_mnemonic": "When a vocab is a single kanji and all alone like this, it's usually going to use the kun'yomi. Since you don't know the kun'yomi reading for this kanji yet, let's use a mnemonic to learn it.\n\nWhat does a <vocabulary>person</vocabulary> hate more than anything? They hate extreme <reading>heat</reading> (ひと). You can always put on more clothes to stay warm, but when the heat gets too high, you can only take off so much.",
   "context_sentences": [
    {
     "en": "This person is Koichi.",
     "ja": "この人がコウイチです。"
    },
    {
     "en": "Is that person a cleaning person?",
     "ja": "あの人はクリーニングの人ですか？"
    },
    {
     "en": "There were many people on Mt. Fuji.",
     "ja": "ふじ山の上には、たくさん人がいましたよ。"
